## Remaining merge gates

- reconcile constants and schemas with the final `2026-07-28` specification;
- run official SDK/conformance interoperability checks;
- verify Linux/macOS CI and binary-cache publication;
- keep safe stdio probing as a separately scoped follow-up.

## Acceptance criteria

- connection mode and protocol version remain independent;
- no request is routed based only on connection mode;
- modern HTTP performs no initialize handshake and sends no session ID;
- initialize-era HTTP remains compatible with sessionful and sessionless servers;
- explicit stateless mode never retains a session ID;
- modern errors cannot be mistaken for legacy fallback signals;
- existing stdio users remain on the compatible default path;
- native, JS, wasm, E2E, benchmark, and Nix checks pass.

